-- ----- fragment: minion_genesis_34.sql (Genesis 34) -----
-- Chapter: Genesis 34 — DINAH AND SHECHEM, THE DEFILEMENT AND THE SWORD OF SIMEON AND LEVI: Dinah the daughter of Leah goes out to see the daughters of the land; Shechem the Hivite prince takes her, lies with her, and defiles her; his soul cleaves to her and he asks for her to wife; Jacob holds his peace until his sons return; the sons are grieved that he has "wrought folly in Yashar'el (Israel)"; Hamor and Shechem offer marriages, dwelling, trade, possessions — "we will become one people"; ★ the sons of Jacob answer DECEITFULLY, making the covenant of circumcision a snare ("to give our sister to one that is uncircumcised... were a reproach unto us"); the men of the city are circumcised; ★★ on the third day, sore, Simeon and Levi take each man his sword, come upon the city boldly, and slay all the males, slaying Hamor and Shechem, taking Dinah, spoiling the city; Jacob's rebuke — "Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land"; the sons answer, "Should he deal with our sister as with an harlot?"
-- Tag: ge34   Temp view: _s301_ge34_lookup
-- Sort band: base 20825, step 3 -> threads at 20825, 20828, 20831, 20834, 20837, 20840 (6 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','genesis',34,v
--
-- Genesis 34 coverage:
--   ★ v.1-7 (Dinah went out; Shechem took her, lay with her, defiled her; his soul clave unto Dinah; the sons grieved — he had wrought folly in Yashar'el in lying with Jacob's daughter; which thing ought not to be done)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the defilement/folly is carried by the extras parallel and by the holy-seed/defilement weave at THREAD 5; no clean NT lateral to the act itself)
--        Extras: Jubilees 30:2 (there they carried off Dinah... and he lay with her and defiled her); Jasher 33:11 (he sent and had her taken by force... he seized her forcibly and lay with her and humbled her) — THREAD 1 (the defilement)
--        Tanakh: none warranted distinct here (the "folly wrought in Yashar'el" register is held in THREAD 1 prose; the consequence-word goes to THREAD 4 Genesis 49)
--   ★ v.8-12 (Hamor: give her to wife; make marriages, give/take daughters, dwell, trade, get possessions; we will become one people; Shechem: ask never so much dowry)
--        NT:     2 Corinthians 6:14 (Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers); 6:17 (come out from among them, and be ye separate) — THREAD 5 (load-bearing: the be-separate / not-mingled register, the offer to "become one people" with the nations refused)
--        Extras: Jubilees 30:11 (command the children of Yashar'el... not to give their daughters to the nations, and not to take for their sons any of the daughters of the nations); 30:13 (it is a reproach to Yashar'el, to those who give, and to those who take the daughters of the nations) — THREAD 5
--        Tanakh: none warranted distinct beyond THREAD 5's NT come-out weave (the Deuteronomy 7 not-intermarry command belongs to its own pack)
--   ★ v.13-19 (the sons answered DECEITFULLY... because he had defiled Dinah their sister; we cannot give our sister to one uncircumcised — a reproach; if every male be circumcised... we will become one people; their words pleased Hamor and Shechem)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the deceit/snare has no clean NT lateral that is not forced)
--        Extras: Jubilees 30:11 (how the sons of Jacob spake, saying: "We shall not give our daughter to a man who is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach to us"); Jasher 33:29 (Simeon and Levi answered Hamor and Shechem his son deceitfully) — THREAD 2 (the covenant-sign made a snare)
--        Tanakh: none warranted distinct (the deceit is narrative; its consequence is the curse of THREAD 4)
--   v.20-24 (Hamor and Shechem at the gate; these men are peaceable; shall not their cattle and substance be ours? every male circumcised)
--        NT:     none warranted   Extras: Jasher 33:47-52 narrative parallel (the gate, the assembling, the circumcising) — narrative coda, not framework-load-bearing as a distinct member; the snare-verse 33:29 stands for THREAD 2
--        Tanakh: none warranted (the gate-assembly is narrative; "shall not their cattle... be ours" exposes the men of Shechem's own gain-motive, recorded but not bound)
--   ★★ v.25-29 (on the third day, when sore, Simeon and Levi took each man his sword, came upon the city boldly, slew all the males; slew Hamor and Shechem; took Dinah; spoiled the city, because they had defiled their sister; took sheep, oxen, asses, wealth, little ones, wives captive)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the sword is condemned excess — NO model; no NT lateral that would dignify it; Red Line #7 VICTIMS-NOT-ENEMIES governs the prose)
--        Extras: Jasher 34:23 (Simeon and Levi swore... by this time tomorrow, there shall not be a remnant left in the whole city); Jasher 34:27 (Simeon and Levi slew all the city; they left not a male remaining); Jubilees 30:4 (Simeon and Levi came unexpectedly... and slew all the men whom they found in it) — THREAD 3 (the sword of the two brothers)
--        Tanakh: ★ Genesis 49:5-7 — the curse on the anger traces straight to this act — THREAD 4 (the deathbed word)
--   ★★ v.30-31 (Jacob: Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land... I being few in number, they shall gather... and slay me; the sons: Should he deal with our sister as with an harlot?)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct
--        Extras: Jasher 34:32-34 (Jacob: What is this that you have done to me?... the sons: shall he deal with our sister as with a harlot in the streets?) — narrative parallel to THREAD 3/4 (held in THREAD 3/4 prose, not forced as a separate member; the load-bearing extras members are the sword-verses)
--        Tanakh: ★★ Genesis 49:5 (Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations); 49:6 (in their anger they slew a man, and in their selfwill they digged down a wall); 49:7 (Cursed be their anger... I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Yashar'el) — THREAD 4 (the curse that answers "ye have troubled me")
--   ★ LEVI'S ZEAL re-weighed (v.25, the Levite who wielded the sword) — Jubilees alone reckons Levi's act for righteousness/priesthood; weighed carefully through Red Line #7 (the point is the seed kept undefiled and zeal-for-Yahuah, NOT the bloodshed glorified)
--        Extras: Jubilees 30:18 (the seed of Levi was chosen for the priesthood... for he was zealous to execute righteousness and judgment and vengeance); Jubilees 30:23 (a writing was recorded in their favour in heaven that they had executed righteousness and uprightness and vengeance on the sinners) — THREAD 6
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
--   1. genesis-34-dinah-defiled-folly-wrought-in-yashar-el — Extras (Jubilees, Jasher) [extras] (the defilement; folly in Yashar'el)
--   2. genesis-34-the-covenant-of-circumcision-used-as-a-snare — Extras (Jubilees, Jasher) [extras] (the deceitful answer; the covenant-sign made a snare)
--   3. genesis-34-simeon-and-levi-took-each-man-his-sword — Extras (Jasher, Jubilees) [extras] (★★ the sword — condemned excess, NEVER a model)
--   4. genesis-34-cursed-be-their-anger-divided-and-scattered — Tanakh (Genesis 49) [free] (★★ the deathbed curse that traces to this chapter)
--   5. genesis-34-the-holy-seed-not-mingled-with-the-nations — NT (2 Corinthians) + Extras (Jubilees) [extras] (the seed kept undefiled; come-out/be-separate)
--   6. genesis-34-levi-zealous-reckoned-for-righteousness — Extras (Jubilees) [extras] (Levi's zeal reckoned to priesthood — weighed through Red Line #7)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★★ THE SWORD IS CONDEMNED EXCESS, NEVER A MODEL (THREADS 3 & 4 — Red Line #7, VICTIMS-NOT-ENEMIES). Simeon and Levi *took each man his sword, and came upon the city boldly, and slew all the males* (34:25). The framework does NOT dignify this as righteous ethnic violence. Jacob himself rebukes it — *Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land* (34:30) — and on his deathbed turns it to a curse: *Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations... Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce; and their wrath, for it was cruel: I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Yashar'el (Israel)* (Genesis 49:5,7). The cursed-anger that scatters the two tribes traces STRAIGHT back to this chapter. The point of the chapter is the holy seed kept from defilement by the nations (THREAD 5), NOT the slaughter of a people; the brothers' zeal-without-restraint is judged, not held up. Systems of defilement are refused; peoples are not to be put to the sword.
--   ★★ THE CURSE TRACED HOME (THREAD 4): the bound source verses are 34:30-31 (the rebuke and the sons' retort) answered by Genesis 49:5-7 (the curse). This is the load-bearing Tanakh lateral the brief names — the fierce anger of Shechem becomes the prophetic word that divides Simeon and Levi in Yashar'el. (Note the providence: Levi's scattering becomes the priesthood scattered THROUGH the tribes — see THREAD 6 — judgment turned to service.)
--   ★ THE HOLY SEED NOT MINGLED BY FORCE OR DEFILEMENT (THREAD 5): Hamor's offer is *make ye marriages with us, and give your daughters unto us, and take our daughters unto you... we will become one people* (34:9,16). Jubilees reads the whole episode as the Law's testimony against giving/taking daughters of the nations — *command the children of Yashar'el (Israel)... not to give their daughters to the nations, and not to take for their sons any of the daughters of the nations* (Jubilees 30:11). Woven FORWARD to the be-separate register: *Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers* (2 Corinthians 6:14), *come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith Yahuah (Lord), and touch not the unclean thing* (2 Corinthians 6:17). Framed strictly as the SEED kept undefiled and set-apart (the covenant lineage AND covenant-word together, Red Line #1) — never as a charter for violence, never as Jew-hatred or nation-hatred; the unclean THING is touched-not, the people are not slain.
--   ★ LEVI'S ZEAL RE-WEIGHED (THREAD 6 — handled with care): Jubilees alone reckons the act *for righteousness* and ties Levi's *zealous to execute righteousness and judgment and vengeance* (Jubilees 30:18) to the choosing of Levi for the priesthood. This stands in tension with Jacob's curse (THREAD 4). The framework holds BOTH without flattening: the bloodshed is judged (the curse stands), yet the zeal-for-the-holiness-of-the-seed is what Jubilees presses, and the scattering of Levi is providentially turned into the priesthood distributed through Yashar'el. THREAD 6 quotes Jubilees as the restored witness's own reading — the zeal, not the slaughter, is what is reckoned — and the prose names the tension rather than glorifying the sword. NO endorsement of the violence; the honour is on the refusal to let the holy seed be defiled.
--   EXTRAS hygiene: Jubilees 30 carries skipped/run-on verse numbers (7,12,17,22 merged in this parse) — only CLEAN witnesses quoted as members (30:2,4,6,11,13,18,23). Jubilees DOUBLE-WRITTEN 'jubilees','jubilees'. Jasher 33-34 carry the extended Shechem account cleanly — members 33:11,33:29,34:23,34:27. Jasher DOUBLE-WRITTEN 'jasher','jasher'. The gate-assembly (Jasher 33:47-52), Jacob's rebuke parallel (Jasher 34:32-34), and the Tapnach-war aftermath (Jasher 34:38ff) are narrative codas, deliberately NOT forced as members.
--   VERSES WITH NO ADD: v.20-24 (Hamor and Shechem at the gate persuading their city; "shall not their cattle... be ours") — narrative bridge exposing the Shechemites' own gain-motive; no framework-bearing target warranted that is not already carried by THREADS 2/3. The deceit-verse (34:13) anchors THREAD 2; the gate-scene is its consequence, not a separate weave.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s301_ge34_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1: Dinah defiled — folly wrought in Yashar'el
    ('canon','genesis',34,2,'jubilees','jubilees',30,2,'extras',
      E'*And there they carried off Dinah, the daughter of Jacob, into the house of Shechem, the son of Hamor, the Hivite, the prince of the land, and he lay with her and defiled her, and she was a little girl, a child of twelve years* (Jubilees 30:2). The restored witness keeps the defilement entire — *he lay with her and defiled her* — matching *Shechem the son of Hamor the Hivite, prince of the country, saw her, he took her, and lay with her, and defiled her* (Genesis 34:2), and adds the weight of her youth, a child carried off. The holy seed-line of Jacob is violated by the prince of the nations.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,2,'jasher','jasher',33,11,'extras',
      E'*And he sent and had her taken by force, and Dinah came to the house of Shechem and he seized her forcibly and lay with her and humbled her, and he loved her exceedingly and placed her in his house* (Jasher 33:11). The extended witness names the force plainly — *taken by force... he seized her forcibly and lay with her and humbled her* — the same act as *he took her, and lay with her, and defiled her* (Genesis 34:2). The love that follows does not undo the violation; the daughter of Jacob is taken against the covenant by the hand of the land.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,7,'jubilees','jubilees',30,5,'extras',
      E'*And thus let it not again be done from henceforth that a daughter of Yashar''el (Israel) be defiled; for judgment is ordained in heaven against them that they should destroy with the sword all the men of the Shechemites because they had wrought shame in Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 30:5). The restored witness echoes the very charge of *he had wrought folly in Yashar''el (Israel) in lying with Jacob''s daughter; which thing ought not to be done* (Genesis 34:7) — *they had wrought shame in Yashar''el*. The defiling of a daughter of the covenant is no private wrong but a shame against the whole set-apart people.'),

    -- THREAD 2: The covenant of circumcision used as a snare (the deceitful answer)
    ('canon','genesis',34,13,'jasher','jasher',33,29,'extras',
      E'*And Simeon and Levi answered Hamor and Shechem his son deceitfully, saying, All you have spoken to us we will do for you* (Jasher 33:29). The extended witness names the deceit and names the men — *Simeon and Levi answered... deceitfully* — the same guile as *the sons of Jacob answered Shechem and Hamor his father deceitfully... because he had defiled Dinah their sister* (Genesis 34:13). The same two brothers who frame the snare are the two who later draw the sword; the deceit and the slaughter are one stratagem.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,14,'jubilees','jubilees',30,11,'extras',
      E'*And do you, Moses, command the children of Yashar''el (Israel) and exhort them not to give their daughters to the nations, and not to take for their sons any of the daughters of the nations, for this is abominable before Yahuah (God). For this reason I have written for you in the words of the Law all the deeds of the Shechemites, which they wrought against Dinah, and how the sons of Jacob spake, saying: "We shall not give our daughter to a man who is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach to us."* (Jubilees 30:11). The restored witness quotes the sons'' own answer back — *We shall not give our daughter to a man who is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach to us* — the very words of *We cannot do this thing, to give our sister to one that is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach unto us* (Genesis 34:14). The covenant-sign that marks the seed is here turned into the terms of a snare.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★★): Simeon and Levi took each man his sword (the sword — condemned excess, NEVER a model)
    ('canon','genesis',34,25,'jasher','jasher',34,23,'extras',
      E'*And Simeon and Levi swore and said, As Yahuah (the Lord) lives, the Elohim (God) of the whole earth, by this time tomorrow, there shall not be a remnant left in the whole city* (Jasher 34:23). The extended witness gives the oath behind the deed — *there shall not be a remnant left in the whole city* — that is carried out in *two of the sons of Jacob, Simeon and Levi, Dinah''s brethren, took each man his sword, and came upon the city boldly, and slew all the males* (Genesis 34:25). The vow is total destruction; the framework records the fierceness that Jacob will curse, never a pattern to follow.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,25,'jasher','jasher',34,27,'extras',
      E'*And Simeon and Levi slew all the city; they left not a male remaining in the whole city* (Jasher 34:27). The extended witness sums the slaughter — *slew all the city; they left not a male remaining* — the same totality as *came upon the city boldly, and slew all the males* (Genesis 34:25). This is the excess the deathbed word condemns; the sword that leaves no remnant is the *instruments of cruelty* and *fierce* anger Jacob will not bless.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,25,'jubilees','jubilees',30,4,'extras',
      E'*And Simeon and Levi came unexpectedly to Shechem and executed judgment on all the men of Shechem, and slew all the men whom they found in it, and left not a single one remaining in it: they slew all in torments because they had dishonoured their sister Dinah* (Jubilees 30:4). The restored witness names the two brothers and the motive — *slew all the men... because they had dishonoured their sister Dinah* — matching *Simeon and Levi, Dinah''s brethren, took each man his sword... and slew all the males* (Genesis 34:25). The provocation was real defilement; the answer was wrath without restraint, the very anger the curse of Genesis 49 traces home.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★★): Cursed be their anger — I will divide them in Jacob and scatter them in Yashar'el
    ('canon','genesis',34,30,'canon','genesis',49,5,'free',
      E'*Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations* (Genesis 49:5). On his deathbed Jacob looks back at this very day and names the two brothers together — *Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations* — the sword-work that drew the rebuke *Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land* (Genesis 34:30). The cruelty in their hands at Shechem is the cruelty the father will not honour.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,30,'canon','genesis',49,6,'free',
      E'*O my soul, come not thou into their secret; unto their assembly, mine honour, be not thou united: for in their anger they slew a man, and in their selfwill they digged down a wall* (Genesis 49:6). Jacob refuses to be joined to the deed — *in their anger they slew a man, and in their selfwill they digged down a wall* — which is the slaying and spoiling of Genesis 34, the act that made him *to stink among the inhabitants of the land* (Genesis 34:30). The father disowns the selfwill that took the sword in his name.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,31,'canon','genesis',49,7,'free',
      E'*Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce; and their wrath, for it was cruel: I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Yashar''el (Israel)* (Genesis 49:7). The sons'' defiant answer — *Should he deal with our sister as with an harlot?* (Genesis 34:31) — is met at the last by the curse upon the anger itself: *Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce... I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Yashar''el*. The wrath of this chapter becomes the prophetic word that scatters the two tribes; the fierceness, however provoked, is judged and not blessed.'),

    -- THREAD 5: The holy seed not mingled with the nations (come out, be ye separate)
    ('canon','genesis',34,9,'jubilees','jubilees',30,11,'extras',
      E'*And do you, Moses, command the children of Yashar''el (Israel) and exhort them not to give their daughters to the nations, and not to take for their sons any of the daughters of the nations, for this is abominable before Yahuah (God)* (Jubilees 30:11). Hamor''s offer — *make ye marriages with us, and give your daughters unto us, and take our daughters unto you* (Genesis 34:9) — is the very thing the restored witness reads the chapter to forbid: *not to give their daughters to the nations, and not to take for their sons any of the daughters of the nations*. The seed is to be kept distinct, not merged into "one people" with the land.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,16,'jubilees','jubilees',30,13,'extras',
      E'*And it is a reproach to Yashar''el (Israel), to those who give, and to those who take the daughters of the nations; for this is unclean and abominable to Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 30:13). The proposal to *become one people* (Genesis 34:16) by giving and taking daughters is named a reproach both ways — *to those who give, and to those who take* — the seed-line guarded from mingling with the nations. The set-apart people is not to dissolve into the land that defiled its daughter.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,9,'canon','2-corinthians',6,14,'free',
      E'*Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers: for what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness? and what communion hath light with darkness?* (2 Corinthians 6:14). The offer to yoke the covenant-house to the nations — *make ye marriages with us... we will become one people* (Genesis 34:9,16) — is the unequal yoke Sha''ul (Paul) warns against: *what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness?* The set-apart seed is not joined to what would defile it; the principle the patriarchs guarded is carried forward whole.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,16,'canon','2-corinthians',6,17,'free',
      E'*Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith Yahuah (Lord), and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you* (2 Corinthians 6:17). Against the merger of *we will become one people* (Genesis 34:16) stands the abiding call — *come out from among them, and be ye separate... and touch not the unclean thing*. The framework reads the chapter''s warning as the holy seed kept set-apart and undefiled, never as a charge to slay the nations; the unclean THING is not touched, and the people are received who keep themselves apart.'),

    -- THREAD 6: Levi zealous — reckoned for righteousness (weighed through Red Line #7)
    ('canon','genesis',34,25,'jubilees','jubilees',30,18,'extras',
      E'*And the seed of Levi was chosen for the priesthood, and to be Levites, that they might minister before Yahuah (God), as we, continually, and that Levi and his sons may be blessed for ever; for he was zealous to execute righteousness and judgment and vengeance on all those who arose against Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 30:18). The restored witness re-weighs the Levite who drew the sword in *Simeon and Levi... took each man his sword* (Genesis 34:25): what is reckoned is not the slaughter but the zeal — *zealous to execute righteousness and judgment* — and the scattering Jacob cursed is providentially turned into the priesthood distributed through Yashar''el. The honour is on the refusal to let the holy seed be defiled, not on the bloodshed.'),
    ('canon','genesis',34,27,'jubilees','jubilees',30,23,'extras',
      E'*And on the day when the sons of Jacob slew Shechem a writing was recorded in their favour in heaven that they had executed righteousness and uprightness and vengeance on the sinners, and it was written for a blessing* (Jubilees 30:23). The restored witness reads the day of *the sons of Jacob came upon the slain, and spoiled the city, because they had defiled their sister* (Genesis 34:27) as zeal for the holiness of the seed — *executed righteousness and uprightness... on the sinners*. This stands in tension with the deathbed curse of Genesis 49:7; the framework holds both — the bloodshed is judged, yet the zeal-against-defilement is what the witness presses — without glorifying the sword.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s301_ge34_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s301_ge34_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-34-dinah-defiled-folly-wrought-in-yashar-el',
       E'Dinah defiled — the folly wrought in Yashar''el',
       E'*And Dinah the daughter of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob, went out to see the daughters of the land* (Genesis 34:1), and the prince of the land took her: *when Shechem the son of Hamor the Hivite, prince of the country, saw her, he took her, and lay with her, and defiled her* (Genesis 34:2). When the sons heard it *the men were grieved, and they were very wroth, because he had wrought folly in Yashar''el (Israel) in lying with Jacob''s daughter; which thing ought not to be done* (Genesis 34:7). The defiling of a daughter of the covenant-line is no private wrong but a shame against the whole set-apart people. The restored witnesses keep the act entire and name its weight: *there they carried off Dinah... and he lay with her and defiled her, and she was a little girl, a child of twelve years* (Jubilees 30:2), and *he seized her forcibly and lay with her and humbled her* (Jasher 33:11) — taken by force, against the covenant, by the hand of the nations. And Jubilees echoes the very charge: *let it not again be done from henceforth that a daughter of Yashar''el (Israel) be defiled... because they had wrought shame in Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 30:5) — the same *folly... wrought in Yashar''el* the brothers named. The holy seed is violated; the chapter turns on what the covenant-people will do with that violation.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20825
  FROM _s301_ge34_lookup sv, _s301_ge34_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=34 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=34 AND ev.verse_number=7
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-34-the-covenant-of-circumcision-used-as-a-snare',
       E'The covenant of circumcision used as a snare — the deceitful answer',
       E'Hamor and Shechem come asking for Dinah and offering merger: *make ye marriages with us, and give your daughters unto us, and take our daughters unto you* (Genesis 34:9). But *the sons of Jacob answered Shechem and Hamor his father deceitfully... because he had defiled Dinah their sister* (Genesis 34:13), and they set the terms as the covenant-sign: *We cannot do this thing, to give our sister to one that is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach unto us... if ye will be as we be, that every male of you be circumcised* (Genesis 34:14-15). The mark that sets the seed apart unto Yahuah is here bent into the terms of a trap. The extended witness names the deceit and the men outright: *Simeon and Levi answered Hamor and Shechem his son deceitfully, saying, All you have spoken to us we will do for you* (Jasher 33:29) — the same two brothers who frame the snare are the two who will draw the sword; the deceit and the slaughter are one stratagem. And the restored witness quotes the sons'' own answer back into the Law: *how the sons of Jacob spake, saying: "We shall not give our daughter to a man who is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach to us"* (Jubilees 30:11). The covenant-sign was given to mark the holy seed; it ought not to have been made a pretext for blood, and the chapter will reckon the cost.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20828
  FROM _s301_ge34_lookup sv, _s301_ge34_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=34 AND sv.verse_number=13
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=34 AND ev.verse_number=14
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-34-simeon-and-levi-took-each-man-his-sword',
       E'Simeon and Levi took each man his sword — the slaughter at Shechem',
       E'*And it came to pass on the third day, when they were sore, that two of the sons of Jacob, Simeon and Levi, Dinah''s brethren, took each man his sword, and came upon the city boldly, and slew all the males* (Genesis 34:25). *And they slew Hamor and Shechem his son with the edge of the sword, and took Dinah out of Shechem''s house, and went out* (Genesis 34:26), and the rest *came upon the slain, and spoiled the city, because they had defiled their sister* (Genesis 34:27). The provocation was real — a daughter of the covenant defiled — but the answer was wrath without restraint. The extended witness gives the oath behind it: *Simeon and Levi swore and said, As Yahuah (the Lord) lives, the Elohim (God) of the whole earth, by this time tomorrow, there shall not be a remnant left in the whole city* (Jasher 34:23), and the deed itself: *Simeon and Levi slew all the city; they left not a male remaining in the whole city* (Jasher 34:27). The restored witness names the two brothers and the motive: *Simeon and Levi came unexpectedly to Shechem... and slew all the men whom they found in it, and left not a single one remaining in it... because they had dishonoured their sister Dinah* (Jubilees 30:4). This is not held up as a model. It is the fierceness that the father will curse — the sword that leaves no remnant, the cruelty Jacob will name *instruments of cruelty* and *fierce* anger on his deathbed (Genesis 49:5,7). Systems of defilement are to be refused; a whole city put to the sword is the excess the framework records to be judged, never to be followed.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20831
  FROM _s301_ge34_lookup sv, _s301_ge34_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=34 AND sv.verse_number=25
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=34 AND ev.verse_number=27
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-34-cursed-be-their-anger-divided-and-scattered',
       E'Cursed be their anger — I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Yashar''el',
       E'Jacob''s rebuke closes the chapter: *Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land, among the Canaanites and the Perizzites: and I being few in number, they shall gather themselves together against me, and slay me; and I shall be destroyed, I and my house* (Genesis 34:30); and the sons answer defiantly, *Should he deal with our sister as with an harlot?* (Genesis 34:31). The chapter leaves the rebuke unanswered — but Jacob answers it at the end of his life. On his deathbed he looks back at this very day: *Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations* (Genesis 49:5). *O my soul, come not thou into their secret; unto their assembly, mine honour, be not thou united: for in their anger they slew a man, and in their selfwill they digged down a wall* (Genesis 49:6) — the slaying and spoiling of Shechem, the selfwill that took the sword in the father''s name. And then the word that seals it: *Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce; and their wrath, for it was cruel: I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Yashar''el (Israel)* (Genesis 49:7). The wrath of this chapter becomes the prophetic word that scatters the two tribes. The anger, however provoked, is judged and not blessed — the cursed-anger of Genesis 34 traced straight home. (And yet the providence of Yahuah turns even the scattering: Levi''s portion becomes the priesthood distributed THROUGH Yashar''el, judgment bent to service.)',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 20834
  FROM _s301_ge34_lookup sv, _s301_ge34_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=34 AND sv.verse_number=30
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=34 AND ev.verse_number=31
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 5
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-34-the-holy-seed-not-mingled-with-the-nations',
       E'The holy seed not mingled with the nations — come out, be ye separate',
       E'Hamor''s whole proposal is a merger of the covenant-house into the land: *make ye marriages with us, and give your daughters unto us, and take our daughters unto you* (Genesis 34:9), *and we will become one people* (Genesis 34:16). The restored witness reads the entire episode as the Law''s standing testimony against exactly this: *command the children of Yashar''el (Israel)... not to give their daughters to the nations, and not to take for their sons any of the daughters of the nations, for this is abominable before Yahuah (God)* (Jubilees 30:11), *and it is a reproach to Yashar''el (Israel), to those who give, and to those who take the daughters of the nations; for this is unclean and abominable* (Jubilees 30:13). The seed of promise — carried by paternal bloodline AND covenant-word together — is to be kept distinct, not dissolved into "one people" with the land that defiled its daughter. And the call is carried forward whole: *Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers: for what fellowship hath righteousness with unrighteousness?* (2 Corinthians 6:14), *Wherefore come out from among them, and be ye separate, saith Yahuah (Lord), and touch not the unclean thing; and I will receive you* (2 Corinthians 6:17). Read carefully: this is the holy seed kept set-apart and undefiled — *touch not the unclean thing* — never a charge to slay the nations. The unclean THING is refused; the people are not put to the sword. The chapter''s sin was answered with blood (THREADS 3-4, judged); its true lesson is the seed guarded from defilement, the come-out-and-be-separate walk.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20837
  FROM _s301_ge34_lookup sv, _s301_ge34_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=34 AND sv.verse_number=9
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=34 AND ev.verse_number=16
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 6
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'genesis-34-levi-zealous-reckoned-for-righteousness',
       E'Levi zealous — the zeal reckoned, the scattering turned to priesthood',
       E'The Levite who drew the sword in *Simeon and Levi... took each man his sword* (Genesis 34:25) stands under Jacob''s curse (Genesis 49:7) — and yet the restored witness re-weighs the day. Jubilees does not glorify the slaughter; it presses the zeal beneath it: *the seed of Levi was chosen for the priesthood, and to be Levites, that they might minister before Yahuah (God)... for he was zealous to execute righteousness and judgment and vengeance on all those who arose against Yashar''el (Israel)* (Jubilees 30:18). *And on the day when the sons of Jacob slew Shechem a writing was recorded in their favour in heaven that they had executed righteousness and uprightness and vengeance on the sinners, and it was written for a blessing* (Jubilees 30:23). The framework holds both witnesses without flattening either: the bloodshed is judged — the deathbed curse of Genesis 49:7 stands, *Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce* — yet what the restored witness reckons is the zeal-against-defilement, the refusal to let a daughter of the holy seed be treated *as with an harlot* (Genesis 34:31). And the scattering Jacob spoke as a curse is bent by Yahuah into the priesthood distributed through all Yashar''el — Levi has no land-portion because Yahuah is his portion, judgment turned to ministry. The honour rests on the holiness of the seed guarded, never on the sword that guarded it wrongly.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'extras', 20840
  FROM _s301_ge34_lookup sv, _s301_ge34_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='genesis' AND sv.chapter_number=34 AND sv.verse_number=25
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='genesis' AND ev.chapter_number=34 AND ev.verse_number=27
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

